The upstream package imports two packages that are `private: true` in its
monorepo and are not published to npm. A standalone fork cannot resolve them,
so the following files are copied verbatim (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 dungsil)
with a provenance header:

| File | Upstream |
| --- | --- |
| `src/vendor/rpc.ts` | `@dungsil/dsh-plugin-server@0.0.0`, `tools/plugin-server/src/rpc.ts` |
| `src/vendor/locale.ts` | `@dungsil/dsh-ui@0.0.0`, `tools/ui/src/client.ts` |

No other upstream source is copied beyond the package that was forked. The
T3 Code `request_secret` contract this fork targets was read from
`pingdotgg/t3code`; no T3 Code source is copied.

## Runtime dependencies

At runtime this plugin imports only `@deepseek-ai/*` packages supplied by the
DeepSeek Harness host, plus Node built-ins. It bundles no third-party npm
code and has no native modules.
